# UX workflow: enter step selection, select steps, and inspect copy/paste previews.
# Purpose: validates that step-selection state is immediately visible in the
# sequencer grid, header badge, and action strips.

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen track_focus

# Move normal structure focus from track to page, then to step.
150 tap NAV 60
350 capture screen page_focus
450 tap NAV 60
650 capture screen step_focus

# Enter step selection from step focus.
750 button NAV down
1800 tick
1850 capture screen step_selection_entered
1900 button NAV up
2100 capture screen step_selection_released

# Select visible step 3 with its macro button.
2200 tap MACRO_3 60
2400 capture screen step_3_selected

# Move cursor to step 5 and select it, leaving step 4 unselected.
2500 encoder NAV 2
2700 capture screen cursor_step_5
2800 tap MACRO_5 60
3000 capture screen steps_3_5_selected

# Long-pressing a macro while step selection is active must keep the selection
# context; the Step Editor is opened only from the main sequencer surface.
3100 button MACRO_3 down
4200 tick
4250 capture screen selection_blocks_step_edit_open
4300 button MACRO_3 up
4500 capture screen selection_still_active_after_macro_hold

# Copy the selected steps.
4600 tap BOTTOM_RIGHT 60
4850 capture screen steps_copied

# Move to step 6: paste footprint should preserve the copied gap and preview
# target steps 6 and 8 before paste is armed.
4950 encoder NAV 1
5150 capture screen paste_footprint_step_6
5250 button BOTTOM_RIGHT down
5450 capture screen paste_preview_step_6
6400 tick
6450 capture screen paste_hold_armed
6500 button BOTTOM_RIGHT up
6750 capture screen pasted_steps
